Pupils should be able to:
1. give time to the hour and half;
2. name and arrange days of the week.

Pupils should be able to:
1.  measure the length and/or width of room, table, building and straight edged materials, etc.;
2.  mention importance/benefits of standard units of measurement;
3.  find perimeters of regular figures in metres and centimeters by measurement; 
4. identify perimeter of regular shapes in their environment;

Pupils should be able to :
1.  find missing number in an open sentence;
2.  identify the relationship between:
▪ addition  and subtraction;
3.  solve related quantitative aptitude problems.

Pupils should be able to:
1. identify and count the flat faces of a cube and a cuboid;
2. identify and count the corners of a cube and a cuboid;
3. identify and count the edges of a cube and cuboid;
4. identify objects at home that are cuboids and cubes;
5. identify the curved surfaces of a cylinder;
6. mention three dimensional objects in their homes that are cylinders and spheres.

Pupils should be able to:
1.   sort and classify number of objects in a group or collection;
2.   identify number of objects in a group or collection;
3.   count correctly up to 5;
4.   write correctly number 1-5;
5.   arrange; numbers 1-5 in order of their magnitudes (quantities)

Pupils should be able to:
